      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Quantum error correction showed how quantum information can be protected despite noise, turning a fragile theoretical possibility into a coherent framework for quantum computation.",
        "attribution": "Shor and Steane independently established early coding schemes; Kitaev's topological codes supplied a particularly powerful route to fault tolerance. These are distinct, central contributions.",
        "maturity": "The theoretical principles are well established and have guided decades of experimental progress, though practical fault-tolerant machines remain under development.",
        "uncertainties": [
