        "Charles L. Kane",
        "Eugene J. Mele",
        "Laurens W. Molenkamp"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The quantum spin Hall effect and topological insulators revealed robust electronic phases distinguished by topology, reshaping condensed-matter physics and motivating new materials research.",
        "attribution": "Kane and Mele developed the theoretical framework, while Molenkamp's experiments provided an early decisive realization of the quantum spin Hall effect.",
        "maturity": "The phase and its defining signatures are well established, with a substantial body of experimental and theoretical follow-up.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The broader topological-insulator story includes additional theoretical and experimental contributors not represented among the credited names."
        ]
      }
    },
