      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The detection of high-energy astrophysical neutrinos opened a new observational channel on the extreme universe and connected particle physics with astronomy.",
        "attribution": "Halzen's leadership and sustained work on IceCube were central to realizing the detector and establishing the field, although the observations were made by a large collaboration.",
        "maturity": "The astrophysical signal has been established through multiple analyses and source studies, with the field now developing beyond its initial discovery.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The collective contribution of the IceCube collaboration makes individual credit difficult.",
