      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Theoretical proposals for atomic quantum computation and simulation helped define how controlled quantum systems could process information and model complex physics.",
        "attribution": "Cirac and Zoller made closely connected, influential contributions to the foundations and practical concepts of trapped-ion computing and quantum simulation.",
        "maturity": "The ideas have been realized and extended in experiments, while fault-tolerant quantum computation remains a longer-term goal.",
        "uncertainties": [
